id: pm-todos-checklist-hierarchy
title: Preview marked checklist hierarchy repairs before applying relations
description: "Acceptance: reindenting a marked child produces one native relation change; title similarity never chooses a parent; cycles and deleted parents refuse before writes; compact previews include affected ancestors and children only. Overlap rechecked: Markdown parsing and text/source sessions do not assign reviewed native hierarchy meaning. Reuse SDK graph topology validators, certified reads, verified native history and mutateItem; one field producer drives preview and locked writes. Native staged-copy preview limitations are tracked in pm-todos-hierarchy-readonly-preview. Selected targets are revalidated inside the native item lock; sibling targets retain a documented last-read window. No package journal or frozen recovery plan."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: hierarchy,markdown,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-29T00:32:09.934Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T01:23:16.293Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T00:32:34.510Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against current core public declarations and sibling graph, CSV and beads docs: no marked checklist repair contract exists. Reuse previewItemMutations for native validation and update for persistence, RelationshipGraph for affected topology, verified history for revision guards. Core transactions serialize transactions only (upstream #1620); re-read every guarded target immediately before writes and document the remaining ordinary-writer window. No SDK pin change, no git requirement."
  "2026-10-29T00:41:16.972Z",codex-agent,"Implemented the shared relation planner, strict revision sidecar schema, native staged validation/update path, bounded receipts and hierarchy CLI. Targeted non-git tests already verify single-child reparenting, exact-ID selection, orphan/jump refusals and ordinary-writer ABA boundaries. Apply is deliberately per-item with truthful partial-progress receipts; it has no frozen mutable journal or package-owned lease, and the final SDK read-to-update window remains documented."
  "2026-10-29T00:53:46.451Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: in a disposable copy, reverting rows() to retain baseline targets made the one-child reindent regression fail (changed 0 instead of 1). Restoring the implementation passed the same regression; the package worktree was not mutated. Linked pm tests passed (typecheck and reindent regression). Real public-corpus reads exposed native previewItemMutations EACCES on immutable copied files; follow-up pm-todos-hierarchy-readonly-preview records the exact public signature and searches. No validator bypass or upstream write was made."
  "2026-10-29T00:55:39.035Z",codex-agent,"Read-only public validation measured 104 native items, 104 exported rows, zero skipped, 11189 Markdown bytes and 12293 sidecar bytes. Unchanged preview returned 104 unchanged. Two changed-preview attempts returned native EACCES, retained as a typed SDK limitation; every copied byte remained unchanged, with no git executable available. The corpus came from committed public main at d1202cf41d538ea11dc9a8967c6aabe64a9cf002. Source was only read through git archive."
  "2026-10-29T01:08:15.514Z",codex-agent,"Installed-path validation justified replacing unusable native staged-copy previews with shared core graph validation plus native mutateItem. Preview and the locked callback run one field producer. Every selected history revision is verified again inside the target item lock, and sibling-target races retain their documented last-read window. Host commands use the injected certified reader. The model now also covers moving an existing blocker between two parents, not only add/remove, so the old dependency is removed exactly once."
  "2026-10-29T01:08:54.442Z",codex-agent,"The final public read-only corpus validation now succeeds on both unchanged and changed previews: 104/104 rows exported, zero skipped, 104 unchanged; one relation proposal affects two rows in a 265-byte JSON receipt. No copied bytes changed and git was absent from PATH. Native staged-copy limitations remain a separate follow-up; the feature's shared native-field producer and SDK graph/mutation path avoid them."
  "2026-10-29T01:13:46.037Z",codex-agent,"The installed-artifact native-format state model passed all 500 seeded sequences: Markdown/tasklist projection, todo.txt, pi todo JSON, JSONL and checkbox; both importer names, sync, every exporter, producer validation, producer re-import, older input replay and CRLF variants. Full native documents were read back through the SDK and compared with an independent model, including preserved repaired parents, dependency annotations, body and every untouched native field. SDK date normalization supplies expected deadline values."
  "2026-10-29T01:23:11.579Z",codex-agent,"The final hierarchy model passed all 500 seeded sequences under random configured lifecycle registries and ambient focus. Targeted coverage measured hierarchy.ts at 99.70% lines / 90.98% branches / 100% functions and hierarchy-command.ts at 100% lines / 87.10% branches / 100% functions; full-package unchanged thresholds remain CI's gate. Packed npm-minimum acceptance passed on host 2026.10.23: two hierarchy rows, one applied relation, zero changes on replay; native source recovery and foreign copied-marker refusal also passed. A no-git CLI test fixture's missing declared peer link was corrected before final CI."
